      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n,s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i*n + j]);\n\n    assert(s<n);\n    assert(n<8000);\n    assert(s>0);\n    assert(n>0);\n\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    int totalR = n - s + 1;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        int nthreads = omp_get_num_threads();\n        int start = (tid * totalR) / nthreads;\n        int end = ((tid+1) * totalR) / nthreads;\n\n        std::vector<long long> colSum(n);\n        long long localMax = LLONG_MIN;\n\n        for(int r=start; r<end; ++r) {\n            if(r == start) {\n                // Initialize column sums for rows r..r+s-1\n                for(int c=0;c<n;++c) colSum[c] = 0;\n                for(int i=0;i<s;++i) {\n                    int base = (r+i)*n;\n                    for(int c=0;c<n;++c) colSum[c] += mat[base+c];\n                }\n            } else {\n                // Slide window: remove row r-1, add row r+s-1\n                int oldBase = (r-1)*n;\n                int newBase = (r+s-1)*n;\n                for(int c=0;c<n;++c) colSum[c] += mat[newBase+c] - mat[oldBase+c];\n            }\n\n            // Find max sum of contiguous length s in colSum\n            long long win = 0;\n            for(int c=0;c<s;++c) win += colSum[c];\n            if(win > localMax) localMax = win;\n            for(int c=s;c<n;++c) {\n                win += colSum[c] - colSum[c-s];\n                if(win > localMax) localMax = win;\n            }\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp critical\n        {\n            if(localMax > mxSum) mxSum = localMax;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing the column-prefix-sum approach with a row-sliding-window algorithm parallelized over top rows using contiguous flat matrix storage improves cache locality and reduces memory traffic; static contiguous chunk assignment gives each thread an independent sliding window state, improving work-sharing granularity on 4 cores.",
  "notes": "The new implementation stores the matrix in one flat vector for row-contiguous access. Each thread owns a contiguous range of top rows (manual static partitioning) and maintains its own column-sum array by initializing once at the start of its range and then sliding incrementally across rows. The inner scan over columns finds the maximum length-S window sum in O(N) per row, avoiding the large colPref array and reducing memory traffic. Thread-local maxima are combined via a critical section.",
